/-! # Compact source tensor for the Eighth family (gident2)

The kernel evaluation of the packed source tensor `eighthSrcXW w` dominates the memory of the odd
and
tensor parts of factory identifications.  Its signed field values (all below `2 ^ 13`) are stored
here column by column with `13`-bit fields and re-spaced to field width `w` by grecip's `respace`
(`eighthSrcXT w`).  At width `32` both tensors have equal cross sums (one kernel evaluation of
`eighthSrcXW 32`), hence the same rational tensor (`tensorRat_eq_of_cross`), and the re-spaced
tensor has the same field values at every width: `eighthSrcVecT w` represents family representative
`7` for every `w ≥ 13` (`eighthSrcT_rep`). -/

@[expose] public noncomputable section
